0.40.27
- Replaced full-destination rover route publication with a 0.5 s receding/rolling navigation horizon.
- Each short horizon is re-planned from the robot's current pose and validates completed/partial structures, staged resources, terrain/slope and predicted robot hull motion before it is committed.
- Added deterministic local collision fallback trajectories (lateral, angled and reverse) when the preferred horizon is blocked; fallback remains bounded to the same <=0.5 s planning window.
- Limited fleet conflict prediction to the same 0.5 s horizon and shortened the WAIT/PASS-to-fallback transition so changing traffic is handled locally instead of triggering long full-map searches.
- Robot inspector/debug route rendering now identifies the rolling horizon / local fallback rather than presenting it as a complete trip route.

0.40.26
- Fixed corridor fan ownership so a branch on a corridor between two structures is optimized from only the nearest entrance; this prevents the second pass from flipping the branch into a self-overlapping U-turn.
- Added a corridor self-overlap safety check and a load-time repair for invalid saved corridor topology.
- Corridor placement now suppresses only true duplicate physical links, allowing triangle links and new links between already-blueprinted corridor runs in the same network component.
- Initial corridor-on-corridor blueprint preview now shows only the junction/adapter fitting until a destination is selected.

0.40.22 - Multi-structure robot deadlock recovery; universal SMALL structure tier; mouse-wheel size-only placement.
0.40.4
- Added PAUSE as a fourth game-speed state alongside NORMAL 1X / QUICK 2X / FAST 4X. Pause uses a 0X simulation multiplier so colony time, robots, production and construction stop while the UI/camera remain responsive; +/- cycles PAUSE <-> NORMAL <-> QUICK <-> FAST and the selected state persists through save/load.

0.40.3
- CR-01 carriers now reserve and deliver the complete remaining bill of materials for active constructions, continuing repeated trips until all outstanding demand is staged or covered by fleet reservations.
- All robot locomotion is 50% faster; acceleration, braking and turn rates scale with the new movement speed to preserve smooth route following.
- Construction progress is now continuous inside every welding/build-up operation; HUD percentages and staged wire-mesh reveal advance throughout each builder action instead of only jumping when a full stage commits.

0.19.1
- Returned to plain release.major.minor versioning.
- Ground resource boxes are selectable and show material, amount and condition in an adjacent status frame.
- Added buildable Storage Dome with 100,000 kg material capacity.
- In debug mode, DEL transfers a selected ground resource box into an available completed Storage Dome.

0.19.0-dev.1
- Switched development builds to SemVer prerelease numbering: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-dev.N.
- Demolishing habitat/resource structures drops the materials actually consumed by completed construction stages onto the ground.
- Dropped material piles occupy ground and invalidate overlapping structure placement.
- Normal mode now reserves the remaining staged cost of active construction when validating new builds, preventing material overcommit; debug mode still permits negative stock.

