0.31.10 -> 0.31.11 : construction-site resource deliveries remain visible as staged material boxes until consumed; robot routes are independent and no longer hard-reserved by another robot, with soft path separation and short-horizon reciprocal collision avoidance to prevent fleet deadlocks/stuttering; construction progress frames explicitly use the global UI-scale transform.
0.31.11 -> 0.31.12 : construction rendering is blueprint-only for every incomplete habitat/resource structure/corridor/supply channel/walkway; no filled/material surfaces are emitted before completion, unbuilt geometry is subdued blue, and erected geometry uses brighter substantially thicker blue wireframe lines.
0.31.12 -> 0.31.13 : robot-runtime stabilization; game-speed-independent critically damped robot rendering, stable per-task pickup/delivery/build stations, coarse-grid A* final stand-off connectors and non-orbiting waypoint handling, persistent per-robot recovery service slots, footprint-aware cooperative builder crew limits, local watchdog recovery without fleet-wide waiting, and corrected construction anti-entrapment sequencing that evaluates only newly revealed mesh and evacuates robots to wider exterior safety points before stage commit. Delivered site-buffer resources remain visible as staged boxes and individual robot selection continues to expose task/status, cargo and condition.
0.31.13 -> 0.31.14 : coordinated pre-motion robot route reservations with visible ground routes and deterministic waiting/replanning; builders use fixed construction service stations instead of orbiting/spinning; construction visuals restored as full blue target meshes with progressively replaced yellow installed geometry and bold green completed meshes for habitats, facilities, corridors, supply channels and walkways; construction frames show explicit stage progress.

0.31.14 -> 0.31.15 : hard rendered-hull robot separation with collision-tested turning and post-step overlap repair; co-directional shared routes can operate as spaced convoy lanes while crossing/opposing routes retain right-of-way reservations; CR-01 carriers pre-stage the full remaining construction material backlog, immediately clear completed trip state, and continue accepting follow-up transport work instead of stalling after the first delivery.
0.31.15 -> 0.31.16 : robot autonomy/navigation rewrite; removed reactive steering-fan/retreat motion and replaced it with precomputed spatial A* plus time-expanded cooperative reservation slots inspired by Cooperative A*/SIPP, including explicit planned waits for crossing traffic, swept hull-conflict checks, deterministic fixed-slot execution, and hard no-overlap runtime guards; pickup/construction/Storage Dome service stations now choose hull-safe fleet-separated positions so carriers are never assigned physically impossible destinations; route inspector/ground visualization exposes cooperative travel/hold slots.
0.31.16 -> 0.31.17 : continuous multi-robot traffic overhaul; removed 0.48-second cooperative stop/go slots and render-spring catch-up, replacing them with Theta*-style any-angle route planning, rounded/densified waypoints, full-route fleet trajectory preflight, traffic-weighted alternate lanes, PIBT-inspired dynamic right-of-way aging, continuous reciprocal speed governing and deterministic replan-on-yield without reactive steering/spinning; robot simulation substeps increased to 90 Hz with no dropped FAST-mode remainder; all construction objects are mesh-only with no structure surfaces/textures, retaining blue blueprint / yellow installed / bold green completed wireframes.
0.31.17 -> 0.31.18 : construction-placement and fleet-scheduling stabilization; replaced full-map multi-pass route rasterization with cached corridor-local A* that widens only for required detours, split route-plan budgets between constructors and carriers, rebuilt the starter depot into hull-safe parking plus deterministic material entry/pickup/exit lanes, serialized only same-source pickup traffic, returned idle carriers to clear standby bays, made normal logistics carrier-first with delayed coordinator-only builder fallback, fixed operation stations for each trip, and kept loaded logistics reservations authoritative while blocked. QA covers live second-structure placement with 6 builders + 6 carriers and placement scaling across 16/64/128/256/512 playfields.
0.31.18 -> 0.31.19 : concurrent logistics-lane refinement; BR-02 work stations now follow the actual rotated structure perimeter with ~0.20 m front tool clearance, construction and Storage Dome service positions are hull-reserved before travel, starter-depot same-material trips use a stable staged queue with one-way outer-gate -> lane -> pallet flow and a clear loaded-rover exit, source reservations may queue without double-counting physical stock, fleet prediction integrates actual speed/acceleration rather than assuming instant cruise, carrier site selection balances concurrent construction demand, and any active builder may claim the single stage commit so a delayed original site owner cannot freeze construction. QA places two structures simultaneously with 6 builders + 6 carriers and verifies parallel deliveries/building with zero hull collisions.
0.31.19 -> 0.31.20 : construction logistics handoff overhaul; every site now uses one deterministic visible material drop zone, CR-01s queue/stage/exit around that single apron, BR-02 fallback hauling covers only uncovered stage demand and uses the same drop queue, builders physically collect the current stage bundle from the drop before assembly, every build step is worked from all four structure sides via planned perimeter/corner waypoints, future construction geometry is reserved before segments appear so robots cannot occupy the next-step volume, and carrier depot ownership/queue ageing is stabilized to prevent lane deadlocks during ongoing construction.
0.31.20 -> 0.40.0 : baseline architecture refactor; the game build is partitioned into explicit CMake implementation/context clusters (app, interaction, rendering, UI, construction, robots, pathfinding, simulation, world core, habitats, resources, networks), with a compact cluster map and next-chat baseline context. Robot geometry search is extracted from the monolithic autonomy system into `game_cluster_pathfinding` behind floor/occupancy/segment/traffic callbacks. Route resolution adds a hard 2.0 s watchdog: repeated local replans do not reset it, and after the timeout the rover discards local traffic assumptions and performs a full-width world-geometry route search while runtime hull collision enforcement remains active.

0.40.0 -> 0.40.1 : fixed construction-route deadlocks reproduced from 001-construction-stuck.gmsave; future-segment collision tests now reject degenerate X/Z triangle projections robustly, preventing distant vertical walls from becoming invisible map-wide blockers. Route clearing no longer cancels the 2 s full-resolution escalation through cleared stop-radius metadata. Starter-pallet reservations gain a final lease break if mandatory recovery still cannot move the front rover, and nose-to-nose fleet deadlocks use a deterministic hull-safe pull-aside waypoint for the lower-priority rover before both robots resume their original tasks.
0.40.1 -> 0.40.2 : fixed the no-building.gmsave construction loop and non-holonomic robot sliding; idle CR-01s now vacate active construction approaches into deterministic standby bays and active construction traffic has right-of-way over idle parking traffic. Route execution aligns the chassis to the actual next displacement before translation, allows collision-safe in-place rotation inside soft traffic clearance, and limits emergency separation to longitudinal forward/reverse motion. Starter-depot loaded egress now uses per-load hysteresis so a rover cannot oscillate across or stop just short of the exit threshold. Replay of no-building.gmsave advances the previously stuck structure from step 4 through step 9 with zero audited lateral-motion frames.

v0.40.5
- Resource packages are now first-class navigation obstacles using the full rendered robot hull envelope instead of the smaller legacy body radius.
- Ground resource piles, Storage Dome boxes and visible construction-site staging boxes are avoided by route planning and continuous motion.
- Construction-site packages were moved into a protected offset staging rack beside the shared drop point so builders/carriers can service the drop without driving through the visible crates.
- Ground-pile pickup service distance now matches the full hull clearance used by pathfinding.
- Global builder work speed increased by 50% for welding/build-up operations; stage counts and material costs are unchanged.

0.40.6
- Fixed a severe robot/pathfinding CPU regression reproduced with slowdown.gmsave.
- Dormant step-0 blueprints are no longer reserved as imminent construction geometry until a constructor actually claims them.
- Removed per-path-candidate construction mesh allocations; collision checks now scan only the revealed triangle ranges in-place.
- Added path-based broad-phase rejection for corridor, utility and walkway construction geometry before detailed triangle collision checks.
- Precomputes loose/staged/storage resource package obstacle poses once per fleet simulation slice instead of rebuilding up to 36 site packages for every A* cell and route sample.
- Keeps physical resource avoidance and future-segment safety while preventing repeated 250-300 ms replanning spikes.

0.40.7
- Reworked robot planning performance around the 0-40-6.gmsave regression.
- Route-search budgets are now reset once per rendered update and shared by all 90 Hz motion substeps.
- Failed full-resolution searches honor a backoff and escalation is edge-triggered instead of retriggering every tick.
- Normal A* widening is distributed across later planning opportunities instead of running three searches in one slice.
- Added cheaper neighbour-edge validation while retaining strict final route and execution collision checks.
- Full recovery searches use a coarser bounded grid to eliminate main-thread frame spikes.
- Builders waiting for materials choose the perimeter sector farthest from the construction drop, keeping CR-01 delivery lanes physically solvable.
- Construction-drop package rows are moved farther from the interaction point so resource collision avoidance does not invalidate the handoff position.

0.40.7 -> 0.40.8 : fixed the 0-40-7.gmsave construction/logistics deadlock and added bounded multicore route sampling. Construction-target robots no longer treat their own target's future geometry as a hard service-path blocker; construction package racks are oriented relative to the target so crates do not cross the carrier exit lane; stale carrier reservations stop suppressing BR-02 self-haul after the 2 s unresolved-path threshold; uncovered site demand triggers near-immediate builder fallback while healthy carrier reservations remain authoritative. Broad/full route searches precompute independent occupancy/traffic grid cells across up to half of the system's logical CPUs while routine short replans remain single-threaded to avoid thread-launch jitter.
v0.40.9
- Added space-time collision avoidance inside path calculation: A*/Theta* rejects route edges whose estimated traversal overlaps another robot's predicted hull.
- Kept continuous execution-time hull checks/speed negotiation as a safety layer after preplanned avoidance.
- Reduced builder construction travel from four perimeter work positions to two opposite positions per stage; the pair rotates between stages and forced corner laps were removed.


0.40.9 -> 0.40.10 : fixed the 0-40-9.gmsave construction deadlock by enforcing dependency-ordered corridor construction: corridors now wait for attached habitats/resources and host corridors to finish, and legacy in-progress assignments are suspended without losing staged/cargo materials. Partially installed structure geometry is now a hard rover obstacle as soon as it becomes visually present, eliminating routes through already-built meshes. Construction sequences are compacted from 10 to 6 stages for habitats/resources, 5 to 3 for corridors, and 3 to 2 for supply channels/walkways; older saves are migrated while preserving consumed-versus-remaining material totals.

0.40.10 -> 0.40.11 : fixed the 0-40-10.gmsave same-pallet logistics deadlock. CR-01 now preempts an empty-cargo BR-02 fallback reservation for the same construction site, BR-02 does not self-haul while an idle/active carrier can service that site, and equal-age starter-depot lane ties prefer the carrier over the constructor. Existing saves with both roles already fetching the same site are reconciled at runtime without losing cargo or delivered materials. Delivered construction boxes are now rendered/staged inside habitat/resource footprints and directly on linear blueprints while the physical rover handoff remains outside the future wall envelope, preventing a delivery vehicle from being sealed into new geometry.
0.40.11 -> 0.40.12 : moved delivered construction inventory from BR-02 ownership to each placed blueprint. CR-01 now keeps supplying every unfinished placed habitat/resource blueprint even when no constructor is assigned, and services dependency-ready corridor/utility/walkway blueprints afterward. Migrates schema-5 saves by transferring constructor site buffers onto their targets. Removed the per-stage BR-02 trip to the external drop apron; staged materials are consumed from the blueprint inventory while BR-02 proceeds directly to safe construction work positions, eliminating the 0-40-11 WAITING MATERIALS stall with a fully supplied site. Save schema is now 6.
0.40.12 -> 0.40.13 : construction mesh progress now starts during the first build iteration for habitats/resources. Fixed BR-02 stage-transition stalls by moving normal work bays outside the next-stage safety envelope, latching evacuation destinations so they cannot hop/replan every simulation slice, and making the hard evacuation fallback reachable after one alternate route attempt. Reduced construction-path CPU load by replacing redundant partial-structure triangle collision scans with the already-authoritative footprint exclusion and by computing mesh-instance sin/cos once per transformed vertex batch instead of once per vertex.
0.40.13 -> 0.40.14 : fixed the 0-40-13.gmsave construction stall and made first-iteration construction visually meaningful. Constructors latch stable work/evacuation positions, partial-structure boundary exits are deterministic, idle carriers no longer spend CPU on cosmetic standby A*, and linear-project work/drop lanes avoid blueprint material piles. Habitat/resource construction reveals a meaningful foundation fraction from the first non-zero build iteration; corridor/utility/walkway mesh reveal begins with fractional stage progress.
0.40.14 -> 0.40.15 : fixed the 0-40-14.gmsave rover-body/structure collision deadlock. Structure/navigation safety now accounts for the complete rendered BR-02/CR-01 chassis envelope instead of only the legacy center radius; a constructor whose hull becomes overlapped by newly revealed geometry performs a monotonic one-way body escape before path planning; completed-structure movement checks sample the enlarged hull; future-stage evacuation uses the full chassis radius with an independent hard-recovery clock; and corridor/utility/walkway work bays are kept outside the full-body next-stage envelope. Construction targets are limited to one active BR-02 each so additional constructors remain available for separate blueprints instead of creating perimeter body conflicts.
0.40.15 -> 0.40.16 : fixed the 0-40-15.gmsave third-site logistics deadlock. Construction delivery aprons are now selected from full-chassis-safe perimeter service points and remain reachable near playfield edges; the mid Storage Dome in the regression save no longer targets an impossible CR-01 center position at z=-31.45. BR-02 is now construction-only: constructors never self-haul and are not assigned or moved toward a blueprint until the complete remaining construction resource plan is physically present in that blueprint's site buffer. Legacy under-supplied/in-flight builder assignments are released so CR-01 can finish shipping without builder/carrier crowding. Starter-depot egress is no longer east-only: loaded carriers select a full-hull-safe exit when a completed structure blocks the normal gate. Completed habitats/resources remain permanent full-body rover obstacles, legacy saves relocate only rovers already overlapping such a footprint, and structures with a planned unfinished corridor are worked from that connector side throughout construction so BR-02 is not sealed onto the wrong side before the next fully-stocked target becomes eligible. Linear construction work bays are full-hull-safe and latched for each build stage so the selected side cannot flip as BR-02 crosses a corridor centerline.
0.40.16 -> 0.40.17 : fixed the 0-40-16.gmsave circular starter-depot deadlock. A BR-02 waiting for a blueprint to become fully stocked can no longer remain parked in the CR-01 pallet ingress/egress spine; idle constructors inside that logistics-reserved zone make only a short, full-hull-checked move to a validated standby bay and still never acquire or move toward a construction target until its complete remaining resource plan is physically delivered. This keeps the strict carrier-first construction rule while guaranteeing the carrier can reach the final pallet that unlocks the builder.
0.40.17 -> 0.40.18 : reworked rover locomotion from stop-turn-segment driving to continuous curved steering. Spatial routes now use wider collision-validated quadratic corner fillets with denser sampling; the route follower looks ahead along the curve, reduces speed according to curvature/heading error, and turns the chassis while translating through ordinary bends instead of enforcing the old 6-degree stop-and-align gate. Short construction/service-apron maneuvers also integrate a collision-checked steering arc. Near-U-turns and emergency traffic escapes may still align in place when required for full-hull safety.
0.40.18 -> 0.40.19 : restored the proven 0.40.17 rover movement executor after the 0.40.18 curved-steering regression caused robots to stall. Kept the existing full-hull collision/deadlock fixes, but reverted the wider arc fillets, denser 0.22 m route sampling and continuous look-ahead steering changes. Reworked synchronous pathfinding performance for construction/logistics: impossible goals are rejected before A*, grid terrain/occupancy samples are cached lazily, route-distance prediction uses binary search, rover path validation no longer invokes the astronaut pressure-volume solver, staged resource obstacles are cached once per fleet slice, pending habitat/resource mesh collision uses a cheap footprint broad phase before triangle tests, and completed corridor footprints use a cheap conservative nav mask. This removes the large main-thread planning spikes seen when corridor construction/logistics begins while preserving the 0.40.17 driving behavior.
0.40.19 -> 0.40.20 : made dependency-ready corridors/network blueprints first-class construction targets and added a mandatory pre-build blueprint evacuation gate. Before BR-02 may acquire or start any untouched habitat, resource structure, corridor, supply channel or walkway, every rover hull must be outside the complete planned footprint/strip; blockers are moved to a validated exterior point with exclusive short-range safety motion. Builder assignment and the first Building transition both re-check the invariant. Dependency-ready corridors are hard-prioritized for CR-01 logistics and fully supplied ready corridors for BR-02 construction; carriers now rescan the global queue after every unload instead of immediately reserving another trip for the same unrelated structure. Linear blueprints use a perpendicular full-hull-safe delivery apron outside the future tube while resource boxes remain visually staged inside the blueprint, preventing corridor deliveries from targeting narrow/unreachable endpoint throats.

0.40.20 -> 0.40.21 : fixed corridor construction work-bay deadlock: linear work bays now require conservative full-body fleet clearance, and persistent watchdog service-slot retries alternate side/along-path selection instead of recomputing the same blocked bay.

0.40.23 - Buried supply channels below rover plane; rover navigation ignores built/partial channel geometry; schema-8 migration lowers legacy channels.

0.40.24: dedicated stationary robot spawn apron; smallest-size placement defaults; flat visible rover-crossable supply channels with schema-9 migration.

0.40.24 -> 0.40.25 : rewrote rover navigation so static A*/Theta* pathfinding no longer treats temporary fleet traffic as world geometry. Added pair-stable right-of-way with explicit WAIT/PASS state, full-hull collision guarding, breadcrumb backout through one-rover-wide sections, first-available passing-pocket selection, and a single-rover detour fallback only after cooperative yielding fails. Tightened the static navigation grid to preserve narrow valid passages, moved the stationary spawn apron beside the starter resource stash, and exposed WAIT/PASS/DETOUR in robot route status.
